   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Displacement\n\nThe frame shears into a grid of tiles that slide out of register with red/blue fringing and film grain, swap to the next scene mid-slide, then settle back. Runs its WebGL shader over two built-in panels (a stat and a bar chart, then a render queue; text and colours from variables), not over the host's scenes: 45 frames of the first panel, a 18-frame transition, then the second panel. To use it between your own scenes, copy the shader into your composition and feed it your two frames as textures.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 3.6 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A cut in a tech or interface demo should read as the picture knocked out of register rather than blended.\n- The rhythm is fast: the whole frame displaces at once, in well under a second.\n- The scenes are structured and graphic, so tiles sliding out of alignment are legible.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want the tearing concentrated in horizontal bands with a hard cut: use glitch-cut.\n- The moment should feel calm or premium: this is a deliberate malfunction; use zoom-blur.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Deploys this week\"\n- value (string): Value, default \"2,481\"\n- bars (string): Bars, default \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"\n- accent (color): Highlight, default \"#a1eebd\"\n- title (string): Title, default \"Render queue\"\n- items (string): Rows, default \"intro-scene.mp4 | Done; feature-tour.mp4 | Rendering; pricing-outro.mp4 | Queued\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#101828\"\n- grid (number, 4-100): Grid, default 60\n- cell_aspect (number, 0.25-4): Cell aspect, default 1\n- shift (number, 0-4): Shift, default 1\n- aberration (number, 0-3): Aberration, default 1\n- grain (number, 0-1): Grain, default 0.5\n- stagger (number, 0-0.85): Stagger, default 0.45\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
